  "_doc": "The weather (docs/wetter_konzept.md). A pure function of the world seed and the world time (WeatherRules), so every peer sees the same sky without a single packet. The weather is a chain of SEGMENTS: each has a state (below), a length in days (a day is 720 s) and a wind direction; the next one is drawn from `next` (weights), shaped by `hour_bias` (time of day, 0 = midnight, 0.5 = noon) and `calm_until`. Between two segments everything blends over `blend` days. States: cloud = how much of the sky is covered (0..1), rain = rain rate, wind = wind strength, storm = thunderstorm strength, fog = mist. `len` = [min, max] length in days. `speed` = how fast the clouds drift in px per second at wind 0 and at wind 1.",
